    "body": "Rework (UMA) for the 2026-11-12T16:13 review.\n\n**Blocker fixed: the shank (`crates/app/src/operation/tap_core.rs`).** `acquit` now records the moves whose full-diameter `Gouge` the core run drops, and for each of those moves carries the core run's body verdicts (`ShankHit`, `SweepHit`, `HolderHit`, `FixtureHit`) into `warns`, one per kind and move. The acquittal covers the thread band only. Body verdicts on moves that were never acquitted are not imported, so a narrower judge cannot add false band-reach flags to a correct tap.\n\n**New pin:** `tap_sim::a_tap_whose_shank_rides_into_the_hole_is_still_convicted`. This is the reviewer's probe: TAP-M6 with `flute_len: 4.0, shank_d: 6.0`, hole record `radius: 3.0`, model half-width 2.5, fed 12 mm. It asserts a blocking `shank/holder at move` warning. I confirmed it fails on the previous head (`[]`, no warning) and passes now.\n\n**Notes:**\n- Cycle check: added. The re-read now applies only to `CycleChoice::Tap | FloatingTap | Auto`. A Tap-kind tool in an explicit Drill/Peck/Bore cycle keeps its full verdict.\n- `a_tap_deeper_than_its_hole_is_still_convicted` and `a_tap_with_no_hole_under_it_is_still_convicted` now assert the `Gouge` (\"cuts past the finish surface\") instead of `!is_empty()`.\n- The #713 sim resolution at Ø4.88 is out of scope here, as noted; verify still holds the post.\n- The `};` indentation of `ctx` is fixed. `generate.rs` stays at +7 lines net. Splitting it is outside this PR.\n- I added the rework decision to `docs/decisions/266-tap-core-verify.md`.\n\n**Gate (final head `458b83b6`, upstream/main already merged, no conflicts):** `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green - app suites (lib + 129 binaries) ok in 619 s, ui suites (5) ok in 88 s, 0 failed. By hand: `tap_sim` 8/8, `tapping_mode` 4/4, `solid_law_goldens` 5/5. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nLeft as a draft. The maintainer re-flags it ready after a re-check.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
